                <pb facs="0224" n="128" sameAs="frus:frus1874/pg128"/>

                <head>No. 83.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Williamson to Mr. Fish.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >United States Legation in Central America</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Punta Arenas, Costa Rica</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1873-12-13"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >December</hi> 13, 1873</date>. (Rec’d Dec. 30.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 75.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose you
                    correspondence had this day with President Guardia. In nay opinion it was better
                    to reply officially to his unofficial note. His letter to President Barrios was
                    left open for me to read. In fact I should have declined to carry a sealed
                    letter. I have read it. It contains a reiteration of his desire for peace and
                    progress, and his hearty approval of the proposed personal conference.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>GEO. WILLIAMSON.</signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d85-a1.xml" xpointer="d85-a1"/>
                <xi:include href="d85-a2.xml" xpointer="d85-a2"/>
